Title: update-publist: search HAL for an existing record before any SWORD POST
Created: 2026-11-09
Author: haduong

--- log ---
2026-11-09T17:06Z haduong created

--- body ---
## Context

2026-11-09, MeSSH slides deposit (hal-05858144): the agent ran the
pre-upload PDF review, the payload gate and the X-test dry run, then the
real POST, and only afterwards, on the author's question « t'es sûr que
c'est pas déjà déposé en une autre version ? », searched HAL, the mail
archive, the project and the homepage bib for an earlier deposit. None
existed, but the order was wrong: a second POST creates a duplicate
record that only a moderator can merge, and the skill's own § 2c says so
without asking for the search that would prevent it.

## Design

Add a step 2a-0 « Prior record check » to `skills/update-publist/SKILL.md`,
before the TEI is built, with its own GATE line:

- Public HAL search by author and title words
  (`authIdHal_s:minh-ha-duong AND title_t:(...)`), and by the companion
  work's `seeAlso` when the deposit is a slide deck or a translation.
- The private side the public API does not show: `Ha-Duong.bib` for an
  `eprint` on the same object or its companion, the project's STATE.md,
  the dated `release/` folders of the object, the mail archive for a HAL
  acknowledgement carrying the title (the `email` skill's paths).
- Outcome written in the release record: `prior_deposit_check` with
  what was searched and what was found. A hit routes to `PUT
  /sword/hal/{id}` (new version) or to the author, never to a POST.

## Exit criteria

- [ ] SKILL.md carries the step and its gate, before 2a
- [ ] The release record template names `prior_deposit_check`
- [ ] Hygiene tests pass
